I left out the logging and metadata-fetch requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read`, so writing to `/var/log/aap/` or calling the metadata service would need capabilities this node doesn't have. The metadata call would also send each item's text to an external host, which is a data-exfiltration path. Operations should request those as separate, explicitly granted nodes.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

